SUMMARY:Deadline: EXTRA Residency 2027: Book-Object on Architecture\, Publi
 shing and Pedagogy (EUR 6\,000 bursary\, Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux)
DESCRIPTION:EXTRA\, a Bordeaux association that publishes book-objects abou
 t space\, invites proposals for a residency to create a book-object at the
  crossroads of architecture\, publishing and pedagogy\, hosted at Fabrique
  POLA in Bordeaux.\n\nOrganisation: EXTRA (Editeur d'espaces)\, hosted at 
 Fabrique POLA\nLocation: Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux\, France. No geographic 
 restriction stated\; the call is published in French.\nAward: EUR 6\,000 b
 ursary (paid in three instalments\; not multiplied for duos or collectives
 )\, up to EUR 500 for materials and up to EUR 1\,000 for travel on receipt
 s\, accommodation covered. No application fee.\nDuration: 4 weeks of resea
 rch and creation between January and June 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.alter
 natif-art.com/appel-a-candidature/residence-extra-2027-livre-objet-archite
 cture-et-pedagogie/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.alternatif-art.com/appel-a-candidature/residence-extra-2027
 -livre-objet-architecture-et-pedagogie/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Fabrique POLA\, Bordeaux\, France. No geographic restriction state
 d\; the call is published in French.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-europe-journalism-partnerships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261105T181829Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20270204T153000Z
DTEND:20270204T160000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: Creative Europe Journalism Partnerships 2027: C
 ollaborations and Pluralism (up to EUR 2-2.5 million per project)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 04 Feb 2027 at 17:00 CET.\n\nCreative Europe's Journalis
 m Partnerships call (CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART) has two topics supporting t
 he news media sector. COLLABORATIONS funds cross-border collaboration and 
 business transformation among news media organisations\; consortia need at
  least three independent entities from three eligible countries.\n\nOrgani
 sation: Creative Europe Cross-sectoral strand (European Commission / EACEA
 )\nLocation: EU Member States and countries associated to Creative Europe.
  For organisations (legal entities) established in an eligible country\; n
 atural persons cannot apply.\nAward: Total EUR 14\,000\,000 (EUR 7\,000\,0
 00 per topic). Collaborations: up to EUR 2\,000\,000 per project at 80 per
 cent funding. Pluralism: up to EUR 2\,500\,000 per project at 90 percent f
 unding\, with re-granting of up to EUR 60\,000 per third party. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Projects normally up to 24 months. Call opened 22 Oct
 ober 2026.\n\nMore: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunitie
 s/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART-PLURA
 LISM?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART-PLURALISM?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States and countries associated to Creative Europe. For 
 organisations (legal entities) established in an eligible country\; natura
 l persons cannot apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ij4eu-investigation-support-scheme-2027-call-2@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261105T181829Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270203
SUMMARY:Deadline: IJ4EU Investigation Support Scheme 2026-27\, Second Call 
 (cross-border investigative journalism)
DESCRIPTION:IJ4EU funds cross-border investigative journalism in the public
  interest\, by teams of journalists and newsrooms working across at least 
 two eligible countries. Eligibility is by country of residence\, not citiz
 enship\; applications are in English.\n\nOrganisation: Investigative Journ
 alism for Europe (IJ4EU): International Press Institute and European Journ
 alism Centre\nLocation: Remote. Teams must include members based in at lea
 st two eligible countries (EU27 plus Albania\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Ge
 orgia\, Iceland\, Liechtenstein\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, 
 Serbia\, Ukraine).\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to 50\,000 per project\, from a EUR 
 1.2 million pot.\nDuration: Project-based cross-border investigation.\n\nM
 ore: https://investigativejournalismforeu.net/grants/investigation-support
 -scheme/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://investigativejournalismforeu.net/grants/investigation-support-s
 cheme/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote. Teams must include members based in at least two eligible 
 countries (EU27 plus Albania\, Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Georgia\, Iceland\
 , Liechtenstein\, Montenegro\, North Macedonia\, Norway\, Serbia\, Ukraine
 ).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
